        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4676af49-d5ec-536a-bc29-156436f27e10",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Henry Bacon, Abraham Lincoln\n- Places: Washington, D.C.\n- Projects: Lincoln Memorial\n- Topics: American national monuments, Beaux-Arts architecture\n\nFacts:\n- Henry Bacon was born on November 28, 1866, and he was an American Beaux-Arts architect.\n- The Lincoln Memorial is an American national monument in Washington, D.C., built to honor Abraham Lincoln, the 16th President of the United States.\n- The Lincoln Memorial was built from 1915 to 1922, and Henry Bacon is best remembered for it as his final project.\n- The Lincoln Memorial was dedicated in 1922.\n- The Lincoln Memorial is one of several monuments built to honor an American president.\n- Henry Bacon died on February 16, 1924.",
